# Copy to .env. Real environment variables take precedence over this file.

# Database (RepoMind's own container, see compose.yaml)
REPOMIND_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://repomind:repomind@127.0.0.1:55432/repomind

# Embeddings run locally; the first use downloads the model into .models/
# REPOMIND_EMBEDDING_MODEL=intfloat/multilingual-e5-small

# Only for reproducing the evaluation: local clones of the two evaluated repositories, used by
# `repomind evaluate` and the gold label tests, which skip themselves while these are unset.
# REPOMIND_REPO_STOCKGUARD=C:\path\to\stockguard
# REPOMIND_REPO_SYNCNOTES=C:\path\to\syncnotes

# Optional LLM. Without one, a question returns the closest lines and never an invented answer.
# Two providers: "ollama", the default, for Ollama or any OpenAI-compatible server at REPOMIND_LLM_BASE_URL,
# and "openai" for the OpenAI API, in its own block further down.
# REPOMIND_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# REPOMIND_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11535/v1
# REPOMIND_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b
# qwen2.5:3b also works, on less memory. It chose worse sources in the pilot and never declined.
# REPOMIND_LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional, for a machine with an NVIDIA GPU: the local model then runs partly on it.
# Search, the code view and indexing need no GPU, and the model works without one, more slowly.
# COMPOSE_PATH_SEPARATOR=,
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml,compose.gpu.yaml

# Limits for repositories added by URL in the web app. These are the defaults.
# REPOMIND_INDEX_MAX_REPO_MB=300
# REPOMIND_INDEX_MAX_CLONE_MB=600
# REPOMIND_INDEX_MAX_FILES=20000
# REPOMIND_INDEX_MAX_INDEXABLE_FILES=5000
# REPOMIND_INDEX_MAX_SOURCE_MB=100
# REPOMIND_INDEX_CLONE_SECONDS=300
# REPOMIND_INDEX_TOTAL_SECONDS=1800
# Where those clones are kept. Defaults to .data in the project.
# REPOMIND_DATA_DIR=

# Sending repository code to a non-loopback endpoint must be enabled explicitly.
# REPOMIND_LLM_ALLOW_REMOTE=0

# A larger model on another machine, instead of the local one. Any server that speaks the OpenAI
# chat API works, and so does Ollama on another machine, whose address ends in /v1. Not the OpenAI API
# itself: that has its own block below, and RepoMind refuses api.openai.com without it.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: with a remote model, every question and the lines of code chosen for it leave
# this machine and go to that server. Do not point this at a server you do not trust with the
# repository. The page and the command line say when a remote model is in use.
#
# To use one, replace the two local lines above with these, and keep the key out of Git: .env is
# ignored, and the key is never shown in the page, in the API or in a log.
# REPOMIND_LLM_BASE_URL=https://your-server.example/v1
# REPOMIND_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:14b
# REPOMIND_LLM_API_KEY=
# REPOMIND_LLM_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
# A server with a key may charge. RepoMind refuses to use one until it knows the prices and a budget.
# For a server of your own that costs nothing, leave the prices at 0 and set any budget above 0.
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_TOTAL_COST_USD=1
# A larger model on a slower machine can take a minute for one answer. Seconds, 300 by default.
# REPOMIND_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
# To go back to the local model, restore the two local lines and remove these.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OpenAI API, instead of the local model. Optional, and it costs money.
#
# READ THIS FIRST:
# - Each question, and the lines of code chosen for it, are sent to OpenAI. Lines that may hold a
#   credential are left out first, by rules that can miss what they do not recognise. Use it only for
#   code you may share with OpenAI.
# - RepoMind sends store: false. That asks OpenAI not to keep the exchange for its distillation and
#   evaluation products. It is not a promise that nothing is kept: OpenAI's own data policy decides that.
# - Put the key in .env only, which Git ignores. Never in this file, in a commit or in an issue.
# - RepoMind is for one person on their own machine. It listens on 127.0.0.1 only. Do not put it on
#   the public internet with a key in it.
#
# The address is fixed at https://api.openai.com/v1. Leave REPOMIND_LLM_BASE_URL unset, or set it to that.
# The model and its prices are left blank on purpose. Take both from OpenAI's model list and pricing page
# on the day you set this up: https://platform.openai.com/docs/models and https://openai.com/api/pricing/
# The model check RepoMind makes is free. Only answers cost money.
# REPOMIND_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# REPOMIND_LLM_MODEL=
# REPOMIND_LLM_API_KEY=
# REPOMIND_LLM_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
# US dollars per million tokens, both above 0.
# REPOMIND_LLM_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=
# REPOMIND_LLM_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=
# OpenAI caches the start of a long prompt on its own, and bills each input token at one of three prices:
# uncached (above), read from the cache, or written to it. A cache write is billed instead of the
# uncached price, not on top of it. Take the 30-minute write price: Chat Completions uses that one.
# Required for OpenAI, above 0:
# REPOMIND_LLM_CACHE_WRITE_USD_PER_MTOK=
# Optional. Without it, reads from the cache are counted at the full input price, which is more than they cost:
# REPOMIND_LLM_CACHED_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=
# The budget check counts every input token at the highest of the three prices. When OpenAI does not say how
# a reply's input was split, that reply is counted the same way, and marked as counted at most.
# Above 0. A request that could go over it is not sent, and search keeps working. The AI panel shows what
# RepoMind has counted, which is its own count from these prices and not OpenAI's bill.
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_TOTAL_COST_USD=
# Only for a reasoning model, and only a value that model accepts: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh
# or max. Leave it unset for any other model. A reasoning model's thinking counts against
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS, so use a low effort or raise that limit.
# REPOMIND_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=
# To go back to the local model, remove REPOMIND_LLM_PROVIDER (or set it to ollama) and the key, and
# restore the two local lines. Before the first real request, see docs/openai-first-run.md.

# The local MCP server (python -m repomind.mcp_server), usually set in the MCP client's settings
# instead of here. Both are required: one database, by name only, and the repositories it may show.
# REPOMIND_MCP_DATABASE=repomind_openai_trial
# REPOMIND_MCP_REPOSITORIES=library

# How the model picks lines. "choose" (the default) shows it all passages in one request.
# "judge" is experimental: one request per passage, about three times slower, and not shown to be more accurate.
# REPOMIND_LLM_SELECTION=choose

# Experimental, and off unless set to 1. When the model chooses the declaration of a constant, and a line
# that uses the constant was offered and passes the evidence rule, both are shown: the declaration as the
# model's choice, and the use as a line RepoMind added. The link shows that one line refers to the other.
# It does not show that either answers the question, and on the two test repositories most declarations
# it could accept were not the right source. Leave it off for anything but an experiment.
# REPOMIND_LLM_LINKED_EVIDENCE=0

# Limits enforced before every request
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_CONTEXT_CHUNKS=12
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=4000
# Per request. The reply is a short list of passage ids and at most one sentence.
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=250
# REPOMIND_LLM_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=0
# REPOMIND_LLM_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=0
# REPOMIND_LLM_MAX_TOTAL_COST_USD=0
